## Local launch scripts (workspace root)

The workspace root (not part of any git repo) holds the actual commands used to run
the offload stack on a single NPU node. Each sets `PYTHONPATH` to `vllm/` plus **one of
the `vllm-ascend*` clones** (see the table above) and `vllm serve`s GLM-5.2-Provide-0610-W4A8.

- `prefill_kv_offload.sh` — prefill-side offload via **`AscendStoreConnector`** with
  `backend=memcache`, `use_layerwise=true`, `layerwise_num_shared_buffers=2`. Sources
  `memcache_hybrid`/`memfabric_hybrid` env, starts `mmc_meta_service`, reads
  `memcache_config/mmc-{meta,local}.conf`. Layer-reuse swap of KV to a memcache DRAM
  pool (GVA) + prefix-cache keyed by block hash (`AscendStoreConnector`/`KVPoolWorker`
  under `vllm_ascend/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_pool/ascend_store/`). ⚠️ Its `PYTHONPATH`
  is stale (warning above) — use `prefill_kv_offload_lxs.sh` for a working prefill run.
- `decode_kv_offload.sh` — decode-side offload via **`SFAKVOffloadConnector`** with
  `use_offload=true` + `lru_resident_cache_config` (single-node HBM↔CPU paging, DSA
  sparse attention — see the SFA section below).
- `pd_mix_offload.sh` — PD-mix offload variant (`ASCEND_BUFFER_POOL=4:8`; sources
  `/usr/local/memcache_hybrid/set_env.sh` + `/usr/local/memfabric_hybrid/set_env.sh`; uses a
  `MultiConnector` wrapping `AscendStoreConnector`). Targets `vllm-ascend-pd/`.
- `prefill_kv_offload_lxs.sh` — `_lxs` (author-initials) variant of the prefill script, and the
  **working** one: it targets the canonical `vllm-ascend/`, whereas `prefill_kv_offload.sh`'s
  `PYTHONPATH` is stale (above). Both scripts set `VLLM_ASCEND_ENABLE_FLASHCOMM1=1` — the
  meaningful diff is the clone target, not the flag.
- Driving a running server: `curl.sh` POSTs `@data2.json` to `localhost:8004/v1/completions`
  (model `glm-5`; `data.json` is an older/smaller payload).
- `memcache_config/` — memcache MetaService/LocalService configs (`device_sdma`, DRAM pool).

## Subsystem focus: KV offload in vllm-ascend (SFA)

A major multi-file architecture **not** covered by `vllm-ascend/AGENTS.md`. **SFA = Sparse Flash Attention** (DeepSeek-style MLA + top-k sparse KV selection). The offload subsystem pages KV between NPU HBM and a CPU pinned pool so long contexts fit when HBM is full. MLA models only (GLM5.x, DeepSeek-V3.2 — both MLA + a `DeepseekV32IndexerCache` indexer); standard-attention models do not use this path.

Two layered connectors under `vllm_ascend/distributed/kv_transfer/`, both registered in `__init__.py`:

- **`sfa_kv_offload/`** — *single-node base*. Every full main-MLA block is offloaded HBM→CPU on a side NPU stream (`SFAKVOffloadWorker.start_load_kv`→`process_layer_data`→`save_cpu`, copy in `kv_transfer.py`'s `KVCacheStoreLayerSendingThread`). The **indexer group and the partial last block stay in HBM** (decode appends to the partial). Decode loads top-k back via `prepare_lru_resident_and_load` + `cpu_sparse_attn.cpp` (**address translation only — no attention math on CPU**; the misnomer is legacy) + `memfabric_hybrid.offload.sparse_copy` (the load-back primitive; was `zbal.batch_copy`). The save path still uses torch `.to('cpu')`; `offload.initialize(tp_rank, 64 GB)` boots the per-rank memfabric DRAM pool. Offload policy is fully eager (every full block); what stays in HBM is decided at attention time by a per-request LRU resident window + threshold.
- **`sfa_pd_cpu_offload/`** — *PD-disaggregated layer built ON TOP of the base*. D (`kv_consumer`, `use_offload=true`) pulls P's (`kv_producer`, `use_offload=false`) prefill KV via **memfabric RDMA** into the CPU pool (main MLA) + HBM (indexer + partial). **Pull mode**: D advertises only contact info via a metaserver (HTTP, once/req); per-layer `READ_READY`/`READ_DONE` over ZMQ gates P's KV-buffer reuse. The D-side `SFAPDCpuOffloadConsumerWorker` **composes `SFAKVOffloadWorker`** to reuse the LRU load path. Three channels must not be conflated: metaserver=rendezvous, ZMQ=per-layer control, memfabric=data plane.

Entry points / key invariants:
- Total switch: `ascend_config.use_offload` (`--additional-config '{"use_offload": true}'`). It drives the hybrid MLA+indexer block layout in `worker/model_runner_v1.py::get_kv_cache_spec` (`OffloadMLAAttentionSpec` for main MLA + `AscendMLAAttentionSpec` for indexer; the "glm5.2, pad reused indexer module" comment is there). Scope: `use_offload` gates the **SFA decode** path only — prefill offload via `AscendStoreConnector` does **not** set it (see the three-paths table in `offload-merge-adaptation.md` §0.3).
- Attention stays decoupled: `vllm_ascend/attention/sfa_v1.py::AscendSFAImpl` only calls three helpers in `attention/utils.py` — `wait_for_kv_layer_from_connector`, `maybe_save_kv_layer_to_connector` (end of each layer, the per-layer hand-off), `maybe_prepare_lru_resident_and_load_graph` — plus reads `use_offload`.
- PD role comes from `KVTransferConfig` (`kv_role`, `is_kv_producer`, `is_kv_consumer`); the PD connector branches on these and **asserts P=`use_offload=false`, D=`use_offload=true`** at startup.
- w4a8/w8a8 quantization is orthogonal to offload: it affects the matmul (weights/activations), not the transferred KV (which uses the separate `--kv-cache-dtype`).
- GLM5.2 (`GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM`, MLA + DSA indexer) model backend is split across three layers: vLLM maps it to an **empty subclass** `GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM(DeepseekV2ForCausalLM)` in `vllm/vllm/model_executor/models/deepseek_v2.py` (all logic inherited from DeepseekV2; registered in `models/registry.py`); the Ascend attention/indexer execution is `vllm_ascend/attention/sfa_v1.py::AscendSFAImpl`; the HF reference (config/weights only, not used for inference) is `transformers/models/glm_moe_dsa/`. `--trust-remote-code` is set but the model dir ships no modeling `.py` — it relies on the transformers-native module + the vLLM registry.

